    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "And now joining us here on Powerhouse Politics, Senator Steve Danes, Republican of Montana and a member of the Senate Homeland Security Committee who took a really interesting trip just days before President Trump's summit to Russia to deliver some messages in person right there on Independence Day. Senator, welcome to the show. Thanks for having me. So let's start with the latest from President Trump. He, as you know, gave that that's a pretty, pretty remarkable news conference on Monday, where he seemed to accept the Russian version of events regarding election meddling. You were among many in your party, even, who were critical of this. He went back and tried to clean it up and said that this is all about a dropped contraction, that the word would should have been wouldn't. Does that end it for you? Are you satisfied with this response?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
