    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77300.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "Well, The president has stated most recently he has full confidence in our intelligence community and their conclusions. That matches where I'm at. I think that matches where most senators and members of the House are as well. And it's matches that we sent to the Russians when we were there a couple of weeks ago. We left Washington DC on June 28th. I flew back to Washington to see the morning of the fourth because I needed to be here for the fifth to catch a ride, actually, with President Trump on Air Force One out to Montana for a rally. But that was the largest delegation, congressional delegation, in anyone's memory when we took that visit to St. Petersburg and Moscow. In fact, it was the first congressional delegation to visit Russia in three years. We met with Foreign Minister Lavrov uh... we met with the chairman of the the state doom of really their their legislative body uh... chairman volodin and we sent a very clear message uh... don't interfere in our elections you have interfered don't interfere in the future uh... respect the sovereignty of Ukraine uh... work with us not against us in bringing peace to syria uh... the interaction that we're seeing now mill to mill with uh... chairman the joint jesus staff uh... done for meeting with the russian generals recently to de-conflict in Syria is a very important step. so that the president uh... what he said yesterday was clear that uh... he he believed the conclusions from our intelligence community that russia did interfere in our elections that's where i'm at and that's where the",
