    "turn_text": "Right. Republicans tend to run on being strong abroad, not apologizing for America. for having a strong military, for having a well-funded military, for taking an America-first approach. And yet, you're right, I was struck by a conversation I had with one, ABC News contributor, who's also a former head of intelligence at DHS, who said he was worried that whole press conference made the U.S. look subservient to Russia. And I think Republicans are going to continue to get questions about whether that is true and how that jives with their world view.",
